1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,342
Dante: Fun fact. Canned food lasts
forever.

2
00:00:04,662 --> 00:00:10,955
BUS-E: Ding dong! This is the Last Bus,
Route twelve. Part seven of ten: the cans.

3
00:00:11,275 --> 00:00:15,758
Priya: Dante. Nothing lasts forever.
Especially this can.

4
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:19,808
Dante: This can is from 1994. Vintage.

5
00:00:19,928 --> 00:00:23,449
Priya: It's bulging. That's not vintage.
That's a warning.

6
00:00:23,769 --> 00:00:24,570
Dante: ...I was going to eat it.

7
00:00:25,369 --> 00:00:29,806
Rosa: Pantry Diner. The shelves are full.
Of cans.

8
00:00:30,126 --> 00:00:34,073
Dante: Marcus. Open the bulging can. For
science.

9
00:00:34,193 --> 00:00:35,333
Marcus: Why is it always me?

10
00:00:35,653 --> 00:00:38,442
Marcus: It exploded! It exploded in my
face!

11
00:00:38,562 --> 00:00:39,767
Dante: ...Is that beans?

12
00:00:40,087 --> 00:00:42,515
Teddy: Gary says if it puffs, it's not
lunch.

13
00:00:42,835 --> 00:00:47,218
Priya: Real rule. Bulging, dented or
leaking cans? Throw them away.

14
00:00:47,538 --> 00:00:51,120
Steve: Excuse me. Is that the daily
special?

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:55,352
Rosa: No, Steve. That is Marcus.

16
00:00:55,672 --> 00:00:57,683
Marcus: I smell like 1994.

17
00:00:58,003 --> 00:01:00,683
June: I remember 1994 fondly, dear.

18
00:01:01,003 --> 00:01:05,728
BUS-E: Safe Zone twelve. Population: zero.
Plenty of room. Cozy!

19
00:01:06,048 --> 00:01:12,418
BUS-E: Part seven of ten, the Last Bus,
Route twelve. Next: the water. Follow for part eight.

